    "display_name": "lay-summary-for-cross-disciplinary-teams",
    "summary": "Rewrites technical research content into a structured lay summary that cross-disciplinary teams can quickly understand and act on. Use when the user wants to explain research to colleagues outside their specialty — clinicians, wet-lab scientists, bioinformaticians, product managers, or leadership. Trigger on: \"lay summary\", \"explain my research to the team\", \"non-technical summary\", \"cross-disciplinary summary\", \"translate my findings\", \"align our team on the study\", or any request to communicate research goals, findings, or next steps to a mixed or non-specialist audience. Part of the AIPOCH Academic Writing skill hub. Sits midstream: after research content is clarified, before downstream deliverables like slide decks or graphical abstracts.",
